{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he called the name of that place Mahanaim.</b> Two camps: the camp of Jacob and the camp of the angels. And Scripture equated his camp to the camp of the angels, for the righteous on earth are like the angels in heaven, to do the will of their Maker." "Or <b>Mahanaim</b> alludes to what would come to pass at the receiving of the Torah, for there the angels descended in myriads, and the camp of Israel — sixty myriad — that went forth from him. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: ״מחנה אלהים״ — this is the sixty myriad, corresponding to the camp of Israel. And of this Scripture said (Song 6): ״שובי שובי השולמית שובי שובי ונחזה בך מה תחזו בשולמית כמחולת המחנים״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:56.929217946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}